              "text": "When our town library announced a repair day, I signed up to help. I arrived early, carrying my grandfather's old toolbox and feeling a little (1) _____.\n\nAt the first table, a girl was holding a toy train. One wheel had come off, and she feared that the toy was (2) _____. I examined it and found that a small screw was missing. I did not have the right size, so I asked the volunteer at the next table. He (3) _____ through a box and found one that fitted. Soon the train could (4) _____ across the table again.\n\nLater, an older visitor brought a lamp that would not light. I was ready to take it apart, but another volunteer (5) _____ that we check the bulb first. She replaced it, and the lamp came on. Her suggestion (6) _____ us a great deal of work. I wrote it down because I wanted to (7) _____ it next time.\n\nBy afternoon, the room was busy. Some people brought objects; others came to (8) _____ how repairs were done. I showed a boy how to tighten a loose handle, then let him (9) _____ the tool himself. He turned the screw and gave it a (10) _____. It stayed in place.\n\nAt the end of the day, we counted the objects we had repaired and thanked everyone who had (11) _____. I had expected to work alone at a table. Instead, I had learned to (12) _____ help, listen to advice and share what I knew. As I closed Grandfather's toolbox, I realised that a useful skill can (13) _____ when people pass it on. I was already looking forward to the next repair day, when I could (14) _____ more neighbours and perhaps (15) _____ something new from them.",
